1
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:16,300
What the hell is that?

2
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:22,020
What the hell is that? Is that you?

3
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:32,280
- Boy, you're really not a morning person.     - Just back off!

4
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,530
Get up! Get up! Get up!

5
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,710
What is that noise?

6
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:46,250
You.

7
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:49,960
It's the chick.

8
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:53,210
She's going through some changes.

9
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:55,800
What kind of changes?

10
00:00:55,970 --> 00:00:59,720
Well, the vet seems to think that she's becoming a rooster.

11
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:05,230
We're getting a second opinion.

12
00:01:56,690 --> 00:01:59,360
Hey, what are you doing shopping at 8 in the morning?

13
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:00,740
Well, I've been up since 6...

14
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:03,870
...thanks to somebody's dumb-ass rooster.

15
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:07,200
You guys, you really should get rid of those animals.

16
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:08,790
They shouldn't be in an apartment.

17
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:12,290
Yeah, especially not with all these knives and cookbooks around.

18
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:18,010
All right, I'm gonna go to the fertility doctor and, uh, see if I'm ready...

19
00:02:18,170 --> 00:02:21,180
...to have Frank and Alice's embryo transferred into my uterus.

20
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:24,850
Now, how will they know if you're ready?

21
00:02:25,010 --> 00:02:28,390
Oh, they're just gonna look and see if my endometrial layer is thick.

22
00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:31,060
Oh, I can check that for you.

23
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:33,310
Okay, everyone, think "thick."

24
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,400
Good luck.

25
00:02:36,230 --> 00:02:37,650
- Hey. Wish me luck.     - Hey.

26
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:39,860
- Oh, good luck.     - Good luck.

27
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:43,320
- And I'm still right.     - That is so not true.

28
00:02:43,490 --> 00:02:44,740
What?

29
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:47,240
She's mad because I know today's her laundry day...

30
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:50,120
...and that means she's wearing her old-lady underpants.

31
00:02:52,290 --> 00:02:54,330
I can check that for you.

32
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:58,590
I just can't believe that you think that you and Chandler know me and Rachel...

33
00:02:58,760 --> 00:02:59,840
...better than we know you.

34
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:03,050
Well, we do.

35
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:06,470
You can only eat Tic Tacs in even numbers.

36
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:08,600
Yeah, what's that about?

37
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:12,190
And you. Ross, I believe if you check Rachel's bag...

38
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:15,230
...you will find a half-eaten box of cookies in there.

39
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:21,150
You're good.

40
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,200
These are not.

41
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:27,660
I'm so not impressed. Everybody snacks when they shop.

42
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:28,870
- Yeah.     - Oh, yeah?

43
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:31,330
Ross, how many items left in that bag?

44
00:03:31,870 --> 00:03:33,210
- Five.     - Okay.

45
00:03:33,370 --> 00:03:38,000
Ten bucks says that we can name every item in that bag.

46
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,760
- How many guesses do you get?     - Six.

47
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:42,550
Challenge extended.

48
00:03:44,590 --> 00:03:47,850
- Deal.     - Challenge accepted.

49
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:50,890
All right, we'll start with...

50
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,730
...apples.

51
00:03:52,890 --> 00:03:55,980
We'll be starting with apples.

52
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:00,030
Stop that now.

53
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:03,070
Yes.

54
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,490
Okay. Uh, tortilla chips.

55
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:07,200
- Yogurt.     - Diet soda.

56
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,950
Yes, yes, yes.

57
00:04:11,830 --> 00:04:14,160
- Orange juice.     - No, there's no orange juice in there.

58
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:15,710
- We win.     - Ha, ha.

59
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,580
They have another guess.

60
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:20,710
Okay, well, we won that one.

61
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:23,550
Okay. The last thing is...

62
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,800
Ooh, ooh, ooh.

63
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:30,560
No, no. Not for, like, another two weeks.

64
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:36,770
I got it. Scotch...

65
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,440
...tape.

66
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:45,450
How did you know she would buy Scotch tape?

67
00:04:45,610 --> 00:04:47,820
Well, we used up theirs last night making scary faces.

68
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:51,490
Oh, man.

69
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:54,540
All right. Ten bucks. Fork it over.

70
00:04:54,710 --> 00:04:57,870
Cough it up. Pay the piper.

71
00:04:58,250 --> 00:04:59,750
Give me it.

72
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:03,380
That does not mean you know us better. I want a rematch.

73
00:05:03,550 --> 00:05:07,050
Yeah, and none of these stupid grocery questions. Real personal questions.

74
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:09,550
Yeah. And the winner gets 100 bucks.

75
00:05:10,050 --> 00:05:11,680
Serious?

76
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:13,640
Are you scared?

77
00:05:15,020 --> 00:05:16,520
No.

78
00:05:17,810 --> 00:05:19,900
Okay, who makes up the questions?

79
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,570
Ross will do it.

80
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:24,230
Oh, sure, Ross will do it.

81
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:28,320
It's not like he has a job or a child or a life of his own.

82
00:05:28,490 --> 00:05:30,370
Well, fine. We'll ask Phoebe.

83
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:31,830
No, no, no, I wanna play.

84
00:05:37,370 --> 00:05:40,420
Looks like your uterus is ready for implantation.

85
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:43,300
Oh, I knew it. I knew it. I felt really thick this morning.

86
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:45,880
- Ha, ha.     - Okay, so, what's now?

87
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:48,510
Go get the eggs. Put them in there.

88
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:52,430
Okay. It'll take just a little while to prepare the embryos.

89
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:56,220
- Embryos? As in more than one?     - Mm-hm. Five, actually.

90
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,690
Five? Okay, where am I giving birth...

91
00:05:58,850 --> 00:06:00,850
...in a hospital or a big box under the stairs?

92
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:04,610
Ha, ha. We do five because that gives you a 25-percent chance...

93
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,530
...that at least one will attach.

94
00:06:06,690 --> 00:06:08,610
That's it? Twenty-five percent?

95
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:12,530
That means that it's, like, 75-percent chance of no baby at all?

96
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,740
Yeah, you know, I was thinking, what are the odds...

97
00:06:14,910 --> 00:06:17,700
...if, like, you stuff, like, 200 of them in there?

98
00:06:19,290 --> 00:06:20,870
Sweetie, now...

99
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,920
...she's a woman, not a gumball machine.

100
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:28,170
Okay, well, you know what? Don't worry.

101
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:31,340
I'm gonna do this as many times as it takes to get it right.

102
00:06:31,510 --> 00:06:35,720
Well, see, the thing is, we kind of only have one shot.

103
00:06:35,890 --> 00:06:39,310
Um, it costs $16,000 each time you do this.

104
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:45,070
So, um, we're kind of using all the money we have to do it just this one time.

105
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,900
Whoa.

106
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:51,530
That's... Okay, that's a lot of pressure on me and my uterus.

107
00:06:52,490 --> 00:06:53,780
So... Well, okay.

108
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:58,080
So maybe there's something that I can do, you know, just to make sure I get pregnant.

109
00:06:58,250 --> 00:06:59,660
No, I'm sorry.

110
00:06:59,830 --> 00:07:02,580
Wow, you guys really don't know anything.

111
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:05,590
I know. Why doesn't she get drunk?

112
00:07:05,750 --> 00:07:08,670
That worked for a bunch of girls in my high school.

113
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:17,060
Hey, guys. Do you realize that any minute now...

114
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:18,680
...Phoebe could be pregnant?

115
00:07:18,850 --> 00:07:19,850
I know, I know.

116
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:24,350
- It's such a huge, life-altering thing.     - I know.

117
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:27,230
The test is ready.

118
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:34,660
Okay. Each team will answer 10 questions.

119
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:38,450
The first team to answer the most questions wins.

120
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:42,160
The categories are "Fears And Pet Peeves"...

121
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,330
..."Ancient History"...

122
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:46,000
..."Literature"...

123
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:48,420
...and "It's All Relative."

124
00:07:50,090 --> 00:07:55,300
Now, the coin toss, to see who goes first.

125
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:03,690
Okay.

126
00:08:03,850 --> 00:08:06,730
- Somebody call it this time.     - Yeah.

127
00:08:07,730 --> 00:08:08,820
Tails.

128
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:11,400
- It's heads.     - Yeah!

129
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,990
Gentlemen, pick your category.

130
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:17,070
"Fears And Pet Peeves."

131
00:08:18,030 --> 00:08:21,160
"What is Monica's biggest pet peeve?"

132
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,290
- Animals dressed as humans.     - That's correct.

133
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,460
- Ladies?     - Same category.

134
00:08:28,630 --> 00:08:29,920
Okay.

135
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:34,840
"According to Chandler, what phenomenon scares the bejesus out of him?"

136
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,970
Michael Flatley, Lord of the Dance.

137
00:08:40,350 --> 00:08:41,470
That is correct.

138
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:46,520
The Irish jig guy?

139
00:08:46,730 --> 00:08:50,860
His legs flail about as if independent from his body.

140
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,820
Gentlemen, your pick.

141
00:08:53,990 --> 00:08:55,400
"It's All Relative."

142
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:58,910
"Monica and I had a grandmother who died.

143
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,200
You both went to her funeral.

144
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:02,910
Name that grandmother."

145
00:09:06,330 --> 00:09:09,460
- Nana?     - She has a real name.

146
00:09:10,090 --> 00:09:11,170
- Althea.     - Althea?

147
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:12,670
- What are you doing?     - Took a shot.

148
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:13,880
Shooting with Althea?

149
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:16,590
- Althea is correct.     - Nice shooting.

150
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:21,470
We'll take "Literature."

151
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:26,770
"Every week, the TV Guide comes to Chandler and Joey's apartment.

152
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:30,060
What name appears on the address label?"

153
00:09:30,230 --> 00:09:32,520
Oh! Chandler gets it. It's Chandler Bing.

154
00:09:32,690 --> 00:09:33,730
No.

155
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:38,070
I'm afraid the TV Guide comes to "Chanandler Bong."

156
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,620
I knew that.

157
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:44,790
Rachel, use your head.

158
00:09:46,330 --> 00:09:48,960
Actually, it's Miss Chanandler Bong.

159
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:58,880
Hello, teeny embryos.

160
00:10:00,510 --> 00:10:02,850
Oh, I'm Phoebe Buffay. Hi.

161
00:10:04,350 --> 00:10:08,270
I'm hoping to be your uterus for the next nine months.

162
00:10:09,190 --> 00:10:11,730
You should know that we're doing this for Frank and Alice...

163
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,150
...who you know. You've been there.

164
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,690
Um...

165
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,240
You know, they want you so much.

166
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:22,870
So when you guys get in there, really grab on.

167
00:10:23,490 --> 00:10:27,040
Okay, and I promise that I'll keep you safe and warm...

168
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:30,540
...until, you know, you're ready to have them take you home.

169
00:10:31,830 --> 00:10:33,170
So...

170
00:10:33,710 --> 00:10:34,790
Okay.

171
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:38,970
Oh, and also, next time you see me, if I'm screaming, don't worry.

172
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:41,550
That's what's supposed to happen.

173
00:10:43,390 --> 00:10:45,260
- Ready?     - Uh-huh?

174
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:47,560
Good luck.

175
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:52,900
All right, the score is nine to eight in favor of the guys.

176
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:56,650
Ladies, if you miss this, the game is theirs. Pick your category.

177
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:58,740
"It's All Relative"!

178
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:03,410
- You don't have to shout everything.     - I'm sorry!

179
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:10,210
Ooh. "What is the name of Chandler's father's...

180
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:13,210
...Las Vegas all-male burlesque?"

181
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:16,630
Viva Las Gaygas.

182
00:11:18,550 --> 00:11:20,670
Unfortunately, that is correct.

183
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,510
Yes.

184
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:25,350
All right. We have a tie.

185
00:11:25,510 --> 00:11:29,680
Luckily, I've prepared for such an event.

186
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:33,690
- The Lightning Round.     - Ooh.

187
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:39,480
Thirty seconds. All the questions you can answer.

188
00:11:39,650 --> 00:11:41,530
You guys are dead.

189
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,160
I am so good at Lightning Rounds.

190
00:11:45,950 --> 00:11:48,660
I majored in Lightning Rounds, all right?

191
00:11:48,830 --> 00:11:51,200
- We're gonna destroy you.     - Want to bet?

192
00:11:51,790 --> 00:11:55,080
Oh, I'm so confused as to what we've been doing so far.

193
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:59,800
How about we play for more money? Say 150?

194
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:02,670
One hundred and fifty dollars.

195
00:12:04,090 --> 00:12:06,010
Say 200?

196
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:08,810
Two hundred dollars.

197
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:10,470
You're doing it again.

198
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,310
Excuse me.

199
00:12:12,850 --> 00:12:15,310
- Monica, I don't want to lose $200.     - We won't.

200
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,690
- Okay.     - Three hundred?

201
00:12:17,980 --> 00:12:20,230
- Monica.     - I'm just trying to spice it up.

202
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:23,990
Okay, so then play for some pepper. Stop spending my money.

203
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:26,570
I got it.

204
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:30,080
How about if we win, they have to get rid of the rooster.

205
00:12:30,290 --> 00:12:32,080
Ooh, that's interesting.

206
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:34,330
Hey, no way. That rooster's family.

207
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,790
- Throw in the duck too.     - What do you have against the duck?

208
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:40,000
- It doesn't make noise.     - Well, he gets the other one all riled up.

209
00:12:40,590 --> 00:12:43,300
- Look, we are not...     - All right, hold on.

210
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:46,720
If you win...

211
00:12:46,890 --> 00:12:48,930
...we give up the bird.

212
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:53,350
But if we win...

213
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,690
...we get your apartment.

214
00:12:55,850 --> 00:12:57,770
Ooh!

215
00:12:58,730 --> 00:12:59,770
Deal!

216
00:13:04,530 --> 00:13:07,490
Monica, betting the apartment? I don't know about this.

217
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:10,240
Rachel, I have not missed one question the whole game.

218
00:13:10,410 --> 00:13:11,660
I own this game.

219
00:13:11,830 --> 00:13:13,040
Look at my hand.

220
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:15,250
Why, do you have the answers written on there?

221
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:19,830
No. Steady as a rock. Now, are you with me?

222
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:23,670
- All right, let's do it. Okay.     - Come on.

223
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:26,050
All right. Gentlemen, you're up first.

224
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:27,260
Okay.

225
00:13:27,430 --> 00:13:29,720
You have 30 seconds.

226
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:33,060
The Lightning Round begins...

227
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:34,680
Stop it.

228
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:39,650
Now. "What was Monica's nickname when she was a field-hockey goalie?"

229
00:13:39,810 --> 00:13:41,770
- Big Fat Goalie.     - Correct.

230
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,780
"Rachel claims this is her favorite movie."

231
00:13:46,950 --> 00:13:48,360
- Dangerous Liaisons.     - Correct.

232
00:13:48,530 --> 00:13:51,200
- "Her actual favorite is?"    - Weekend at Bernie's. Correct.

233
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:57,620
"In what part of her body did Monica get a pencil stuck at age 14?"

234
00:13:57,790 --> 00:13:59,080
Oh!

235
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:02,920
Ew, no!

236
00:14:05,210 --> 00:14:06,340
Her ear.

237
00:14:09,590 --> 00:14:13,720
All right, "Monica categorizes her towels. How many categories are there?"

238
00:14:13,890 --> 00:14:15,270
- Okay, everyday use.     - Fancy.

239
00:14:15,430 --> 00:14:16,850
- Guest.     - Fancy guest.

240
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:18,980
- Two seconds.     - Uh, eleven?

241
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:22,360
Eleven. Unbelievable. Eleven is correct.

242
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:23,770
Yes!

243
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,400
All right.

244
00:14:27,570 --> 00:14:29,860
That's four for the guys. Ladies, you're up.

245
00:14:30,030 --> 00:14:31,820
All right, all right, come on!

246
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:37,870
Thirty seconds on the clock.

247
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:40,540
Five correct questions wins the game.

248
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:44,380
The Lightning Round begins now. "What is Joey's favorite food?"

249
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,000
- Sandwiches.     - Correct.

250
00:14:46,170 --> 00:14:48,720
"Chandler was how old when he first touched a girl's breast?"

251
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:50,220
- Fourteen?     - No, 19.

252
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:51,760
Thanks, man.

253
00:14:52,390 --> 00:14:54,600
"Joey had an imaginary childhood friend.

254
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,390
- His name was..."     - Maurice.

255
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:58,140
- "His profession was?"     - Space cowboy.

256
00:14:58,310 --> 00:14:59,600
Correct.

257
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,150
"What is Chandler Bing's job?"

258
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,730
Oh.

259
00:15:07,230 --> 00:15:09,650
